{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And you shall serve HaShem your Elohim, and He will bless your bread.</b> It begins in plural language and concludes in singular language, because all Israel are guarantors for one another, and HaShem will not bless the bread of each and every individual until those who serve HaShem are many and all the seed of Jacob serve Him as one — then the bread of each and every one will be blessed. And some say that the service of HaShem is better when many gather to pray, for ״הֵן אֵל כַּבִּיר לֹא יִמְאָס״ (Job 36:5). But in matters of eating it is better when each person eats his own portion alone. And because most illnesses come through foods from without, or through the predominance of one element over another from within, therefore He said ״וּבֵרַךְ אֶת לַחְמְךָ וְאֶת מֵימֶיךָ וַהֲסִרֹתִי מַחֲלָה מִקִּרְבֶּךָ״ — 'and He will bless your bread and your waters, and I will remove illness from your midst.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:22:30.363072123Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}